WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.400
Two more ideas from the first part of the
book frame everything in this session.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.538
First, the hybrid-join trap.

3
00:00:06.538 --> 00:00:11.387
Converting a domain-joined fleet to hybrid
join is close to a tenant-wide switch.

4
00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:14.221
Extend the sync scope to the computer OUs,

5
00:00:14.221 --> 00:00:17.722
publish a service connection
point in each forest,

6
00:00:17.722 --> 00:00:22.557
or push the same two values by GPO,
and every Windows device's Automatic

7
00:00:22.557 --> 00:00:27.225
Device Join task reads it and
registers itself, retrying every hour.

8
00:00:27.225 --> 00:00:31.813
Nothing in that path checks ownership,
organizational position or approval.

9
00:00:31.813 --> 00:00:36.278
Microsoft's guidance has two halves:
Entra join is the default for new,

10
00:00:36.278 --> 00:00:41.606
refurbished or reset devices; hybrid join
gives existing domain-joined devices a

11
00:00:41.606 --> 00:00:46.699
cloud identity with minimal impact, but it
shouldn't be long term or the end goal.

12
00:00:46.699 --> 00:00:50.548
Converting a hybrid device to
Entra join later needs a reset,

13
00:00:50.548 --> 00:00:55.012
and hybrid devices need periodic line
of sight to a domain controller.

14
00:00:55.012 --> 00:00:58.625
Done ungoverned, the waypoint
becomes the destination.

15
00:00:58.625 --> 00:01:00.763
Second, where the truth lives.

16
00:01:00.763 --> 00:01:06.371
A modern laptop is described by a procurement
record, an Autopilot registration,

17
00:01:06.371 --> 00:01:10.891
an Entra ID device object, an Intune
record and a Defender machine;

18
00:01:10.891 --> 00:01:12.900
a server adds an Arc resource.

19
00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:17.288
The program decides, fact by
fact, which one is authoritative.

20
00:01:17.288 --> 00:01:19.662
Procurement owns the business facts.

21
00:01:19.662 --> 00:01:22.737
The Entra object owns
identity and join type.

22
00:01:22.737 --> 00:01:26.211
Intune owns management
and evaluates compliance;

23
00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:29.024
Entra's is-compliant flag only reports it.

24
00:01:29.024 --> 00:01:31.413
Defender owns threat and exposure.

25
00:01:31.413 --> 00:01:33.400
Arc owns management for servers.

26
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:38.115
Correlate on the right key: the Entra
device ID across Microsoft records,

27
00:01:38.115 --> 00:01:42.437
the serial number to procurement,
and the Azure resource ID for Arc.

28
00:01:42.437 --> 00:01:44.486
And delete the Entra object last,

29
00:01:44.486 --> 00:01:48.190
because deleting it deletes
the BitLocker recovery keys.
